    "execution": "Hash-pinned numeric host at 0x3f0000. Original particles 0x4428a0, built-in images 0x439650, shader creation 0x43c570 and GL_State 0x42aac0. Replaced image, formatting, shader-finalization and GL callbacks; no original entry point or graphics/input/audio/network startup.",
    "incorporation": "Independent implementation from generated numeric and ABI observations. No original implementation, module or image/asset bytes incorporated."
  },
  "contracts": {
    "particle_bytes": 16,
    "renderer_api": 27,
    "surface_type": "SF_IHV_PARTICLES uses frame-owned point storage; each view expands independent triangles.",
    "geometry": "1.5-scaled up/right axes; mirror reverses right sign. Depth accumulated z,x,y. Scale=1 below 20, otherwise 1+depth*.004. Vertex UVs (0,0),(1.125,0),(0,1.125); unchanged RGBA.",
    "image": "16x16 binary RGBA; all channels 255 where (x-5)^2+(y-5)^2<=20, else zero; no mipmaps.",
    "material": "Original shader sort 6, rgb/alpha generator 3, state 0x62. GL callbacks verify ONE/ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA and no depth writes; modern shader uses exact vertex RGBA and normal depth testing.",
    "lifetime": "Copy input synchronously; retain until existing frame storage is reset. Invalid batches and capacity failures do not advance pending scene cursors. No native module pointer retained.",
    "ray": "RTX expands the same per-view triangles through existing material/geometry services and hashes exact camera/mirror state for particle geometry. Ordinary polygon signatures unchanged.",
    "asset_profile_correction": "Prior shader/fog/sky/text-repair/classic-light checks accepted retail Q3 only. They now admit the separate native IHV profile without changing module/network contracts."
  },
